# S0 (QUALIFICATION): the baked serving profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full on the shipping image WITHOUT the audits: the bytes a platform launch serves. Same five tests as A1.
# The smoke action always passes QWEN_C2_PROFILE (the job reader defaults an unset C2_PROFILE to the pair profile general), so the profile is named here; that
# the image BOOTS it by its own default with no profile set is proven by X0B (provenance (c)) and by SR10 (the replay sets none). READ: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full',
# the eight-seat engine, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED; every hash EQUAL to A1's (the audits change nothing) and so to W1's reference. The operator
# builds the thin layer for SR10 after this job passes. Real time ~30.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-full pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of ship/262k-full (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
